From 5097ce6a1ad7b79ec45a784607d5932e3ac07754 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:01:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web: Power on the radio and Power off the radio in the Misc
 menu

The two drawer rows, on the web page: above "Power off the Tab5" in the Misc
menu, and on /api/cmd for other programs:

  {"action":"radio_power_on"}                       -> the NAS relay presses
      the QMX's power button (Remote Power-ON); answers result =
      pressing | on | nocable | busy | usb | noanswer, with a message
  {"action":"radio_power_off","confirm":"RADIOOFF"} -> RX; then PS0;

Power off asks for confirmation, like Power off the Tab5. The drawer and the
web share ui_radio_power_off(), which puts the radio back into receive
first and refuses while no radio is connected or another device has the
transmitter.

Builds; check_web, check_webui, check_tx_guard, check_unattended_tx and
check_drawer_sections are clean. Not yet tested on the Tab5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
